WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-GB

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:01.040
Hi, everyone.

00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:04.020
Tom here, from BBC Learning English in London.

00:00:04.020 --> 00:00:04.780
And today,

00:00:04.780 --> 00:00:08.680
I'm going to tell you what to say after the word wish.

00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:10.840
When we're talking about wishes,

00:00:10.840 --> 00:00:14.200
we're talking about situations that are imaginary

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:15.660
or unreal.

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:18.640
To show this, after saying 'I wish',

00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:22.000
we use the past to talk about the wish,

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:23.640
which is in the present.

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:25.240
So, I could say:

00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:28.940
I wish I had a cup of tea.

00:00:28.940 --> 00:00:31.040
Ah, thank you!

00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:36.060
Now, if we want to make a wish about the past,

00:00:36.060 --> 00:00:39.260
we need to use the 'past past'

00:00:39.260 --> 00:00:41.480
- or the past perfect.

00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:42.660
For example:

00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:45.680
I wish I had chosen

00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:47.440
a more formal shirt

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:50.100
before I filmed this video today.

